      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For decimals, group digits in pairs on both sides of the decimal point.\n\nIf a decimal has an odd number of decimal digits, append a zero.\n\nExample: 0.9 can be written 0.90, then more pairs of zeros can be added when more decimal places are needed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
